<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yelü Dashi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1087">1087</a>–1143</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Emperor Dezong of Western Liao</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yelü Dashi was a Khitan prince of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao dynasty</a> who fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchens">Jurchen</a> in its final years. When the Jurchen Jin destroyed the Liao in 1125 he led followers west into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balasagun">Balasagun</a> and proclaimed himself Gurkhan, founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qara-khitai">Qara Khitai</a>. In 1141 he defeated the Seljuk sultan Sanjar at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-qatwan">Battle of Qatwan</a>.</p></div>
